column27:
When an Abuse report is submitted for a comment ({{/comments/####}}), it should include information about the commenter in the field {{cf_user_id}}. This should not be transmitted via a hidden field on the abuse report form, but rather handled in the controller/model as appropriate. 

Comments by registered users are associated with pseud IDs, so you’ll have to look up the user ID (if it exists) and record that instead.

* If the comment is from a guest, the field should say {{guestcomment}}.
* If the comment is from an extant account, the field should record the user ID (not the pseud ID) as a plain number.
** Exception: if the comment is from orphan_account, the field should say {{orphanedcomment}} instead.
* If the comment is from a deleted account, the field should say {{deletedaccount}}. 
* If the comment is deleted, the field should have {{deletedcomment}} either as the sole text (if it's a 404 page) or appended to the front of the field with a comma (if it's the top-level comment in a thread). 

For the purposes of this issue, we will not collect information from any replies/child comments, only the specific comment ID that is provided in the URL field.

h2. Testing

You will need 2 accounts: 

* Account A, which has multiple pseuds and a work by one of those pseuds that you're willing to orphan
* Account B, which you're willing to delete

PAC will need to verify the expected information is available and correct for all of the following:

# Comment as a guest, then report the comment. The userID field should be {{guestcomment}}
# Comment as Account A on your own work, then orphan the work leaving your pseud on. Confirm that the comment is now associated with "pseud (orphan_account)", then report the comment. The userID field should be {{orphanedcomment}}
# Comment as Account A using your pseud, then report it. The userID field should be {{[A's userID]}}
# Comment as Account B. 
# Reply to all four top-level comments as Account A.
# Report the comment from step 4 (B's comment with a reply from A). The userID field should be {{[B's userID]}}
# Delete account B. Confirm that the top-level comment from step 4 is now associated with "Deleted Account", then report the comment. The userID field should be {{deletedaccount}}
# Delete the top-level guest comment from step 1, then report it. The userID field should be {{deletedcomment, guestcomment}}
# Delete the top-level orphaned comment from step 2, then report it. The userID field should be {{deletedcomment, orphanedcomment}}
# Delete the top-level comment from step 3 (A's comment with a reply from A), then report it. The userID field should be {{deletedcomment, [A's userID]}}
# Delete the top-level comment from step 4 (Deleted Account B's comment with a reply from A), then report it. The userID field should be {{deletedcomment, deletedaccount}}
# Delete one of the reply comments from the previous four steps. Confirm that the top-level comment now 404s, then report it. The userID field should be {{deletedcomment}}

The “Your account has been banned”/”Your account has been suspended” error messages only appear if the banned/suspended user performs a disallowed action. We’d like to also present this text to users logging in to a banned/suspended account.

This will require updating the “Successfully logged in.” messages so that banned/suspended users see a new paragraph consisting of the appropriate text from [locales/controllers/en.yml ban_notice_html and suspension_notice_html|https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/0fc1f84d3d2ebdd5e6b13b8b50849e88876dc5c4/config/locales/controllers/en.yml#L289-L290]. 

h2. Testing

# Log in to an unbanned, unsuspended account without clicking “Remember me”. You should see the following message: 

{noformat}<p>Successfully logged in. <strong>You'll stay logged in for 2 weeks even if you close your browser, so make sure to log out if you're using a public or shared computer.</strong></p>{noformat}

# Log in to testy_banned without clicking “Remember me”. You should see the following message: 

{noformat}<p>Successfully logged in. <strong>You'll stay logged in for 2 weeks even if you close your browser, so make sure to log out if you're using a public or shared computer.</strong></p>
<p>Your account has been banned. You are not permitted to post or edit content on AO3. Please check your email or <a href="https://archiveofourown.org/abuse_reports/new">contact our Policy & Abuse team</a> for more information.</p>{noformat}

# Log in to testy_suspended without clicking “Remember me”. You should see the following message: 

{noformat}<p>Successfully logged in. <strong>You'll stay logged in for 2 weeks even if you close your browser, so make sure to log out if you're using a public or shared computer.</strong></p>
<p>Your account has been suspended until [DAY DD MMM YYYY]. You cannot post, edit, or delete content until your suspension has ended. Please check your email or <a href="https://archiveofourown.org/abuse_reports/new">contact our Policy & Abuse team</a> for more information.</p>{noformat}

# Log in to an unbanned, unsuspended account while also clicking “Remember me”. You should see the following message: 

{noformat}<p>Successfully logged in.</p>{noformat}

# Log in to testy_banned while also clicking “Remember me”. You should see the following message: 

{noformat}<p>Successfully logged in.</p>
<p>Your account has been banned. You are not permitted to post or edit content on AO3. Please check your email or <a href="https://archiveofourown.org/abuse_reports/new">contact our Policy & Abuse team</a> for more information.</p>{noformat}

# Log in to testy_suspended while also clicking “Remember me”. You should see the following message: 

{noformat}<p>Successfully logged in.</p>
<p>Your account has been suspended until [DAY DD MM YYYY]. You cannot post, edit, or delete content until your suspension has ended. Please check your email or <a href="https://archiveofourown.org/abuse_reports/new">contact our Policy & Abuse team</a> for more information.</p>{noformat}

