When viewing the AO3 homepage logged out, the heading currently reads “A fan-created, fan-run, nonprofit, noncommercial archive for transformative fanworks, like fanfiction, fanart, fan videos, and podfic”. 

We’d like to update this text to more closely match the new introduction on [https://www.transformativeworks.org/our-projects/archive-of-our-own/|https://www.transformativeworks.org/our-projects/archive-of-our-own/]: 

{quote}A non-profit, non-commercial archive for transformative fanworks; created by and for fans of books, music, art, games, shows, movies, real-person fiction (RPF), and other fandoms.{quote}

In addition, please add “(AO3)” to the text underneath the statistics line: 

{quote}The Archive of Our Own (AO3) is a project of the Organization for Transformative Works.{quote}

*This should only be picked up by official AD&T volunteers/contractors due to its testing requirements w.r.t. the existing deployment process.*

We want to provide a Docker image that can be run in production environments. (Due to the tools that are helpful for development baked into the existing image, it is not suitable for production contexts.) As part of this, we want to:

# make the actual {{Dockerfile}} ;
# update the Github actions configuration to build the new image and push it to the repository’s container registry;
# test that the application can be run in our production environment, with minimal changes, using the new image

