column27:
h1. Steps to reproduce

# Log in
# Choose an adventure:
## Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > Create Site Skin
## Hi, username! > My Dashboard > Skins > My Work Skins > Create Work Skin
# Enter CSS like {{.a { fill: #900 } .aa { stroke: darkred; } .aaa { stroke-width: 2px; }}}
# Submit

h1. What happens

An error saying the properties are not allowed.

h1. What should happen

It should be possible to make a site or work skin using the [fill CSS property|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/fill] to adjust the fill color of SVG images, [stroke|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/stroke] to adjust the stroke color, and [stroke-width|https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/stroke-width] to adjust the stroke size.

All of the following values should be allowed:

{noformat}fill: darkred;
fill: #900;
fill: rgba(0, 200, 0, 0.5);
fill: hsl(228 4% 24%);
fill: none;
stroke: darkred;
stroke: #900;
stroke: rgba(0 200 0);
stroke: hsl(228 4% 24%);
stroke: none;
stroke-width: 100%;
stroke-width: 1cm;
stroke-width: 1em;
stroke-width: 1ex;
stroke-width: 1in;
stroke-width: 1mm;
stroke-width: 1pc;
stroke-width: 1pt;
stroke-width: 1px;{noformat}

h1. Testing

Put the following into a skin and make sure that after saving, the output matches the input and you don't get any error messages. Note that this won’t actually lead to any visual changes; we’re just trying to make sure all the values are accepted by our system. 

{noformat}.a { fill: darkred; }
.b { fill: #900; }
.c { fill: rgb(0 200 0); }
.d { fill: hsl(228 4% 24%); }
.aa { stroke: darkred; }
.bb { stroke: #900; }
.cc { stroke: rgb(0, 200, 0); }
.dd { stroke: hsl(228 4% 24%); }
.ee { stroke: none; }
.aaa { stroke-width: 100%; }
.bbb { stroke-width: 1cm; }
.ccc { stroke-width: 1em; }
.ddd { stroke-width: 1ex; }
.eee { stroke-width: 1in; } 
.fff { stroke-width: 1mm; }
.hhh { stroke-width: 1pc; }
.iii { stroke-width: 1pt; }
.jjj { stroke-width: 1px; }{noformat}

Additionally, please make sure the following produces error messages about the values not being allowed (there will also be a message saying “There don't seem to be any rules for [selector]”):

{noformat}.a { fill: url("https://ao3.org/image.png"); }
.b { fill: url("https://ao3.org/image.png") darkred; }
.c { fill: url("/image.png"); }
.d { fill: url("/image.png") darkred; }
.aa { stroke: url("https://ao3.org/image.png"); }{noformat}

(The above isn’t strictly necessary to include given how we limit URLs, but color adjustments are the main thing we want to allow, and forbidding {{url()}} is default behavior for us.)

You’ll also need to check the skins help file – the ? by the CSS field – and make sure the new properties are listed.

