*Testing*

Automated tests only

The text on the Muted Users page does not accurately reflect the behavior of the muting function, if the user has a direct link to a work by a muted user.

Page: [https://archiveofourown.org/users/USERNAME/muted/users|https://archiveofourown.org/users/USERNAME/muted/users]

This is the current text of the page:

{{You can mute up to 3,000 users. Muting a user:}}

* {{completely hides their works, series, bookmarks, and comments from you; there will be no empty space, placeholder text, or other indication something has been removed}}

{{Muting a user will not:}}

* {{prevent you from receiving comment or subscription emails from this user}}
* {{hide their works, series, bookmarks, and comments from anyone else}}

Proposal to change the text to (something like) this:

{{You can mute up to 3,000 users. Muting a user:}}

* {{completely hides their works, series, bookmarks, and comments from you while browsing AO3; there will be no empty space, placeholder text, or other indication something has been removed}}

{{Muting a user will not:}}

* {{prevent you from receiving comment or subscription emails from this user}}
* {{prevent you from accessing their profile or their works with a direct link}}
* {{hide their works, series, bookmarks, and comments from anyone else}}

NOTE:

The confirmation page also contains the same text, and will also require the same update. It will appear if you attempt to mute a user directly from their profile, or after entering their username on your Muted Users page and selecting the “Mute” button:

[https://archiveofourown.org/users/USERNAME/muted/users/confirm_mute?muted_id=USERNAME_TO_BE_MUTED|https://archiveofourown.org/users/USERNAME/muted/users/confirm_mute?muted_id=USERNAME_TO_BE_MUTED]

The only difference is the opening sentence:

{{Are you sure you want to mute USERNAME_TO_BE_MUTED? Muting a user:}}

Currently, works in Unrevealed collections have (at the top of the work and in the work blurb) text saying that the work is “part of an ongoing challenge and will be revealed soon!” While this is what Unrevealed collections were intended for, on a practical level they are more frequently being used so creators can “hide” their own works indefinitely without removing them from the site entirely. Therefore, the current text is confusing and often inaccurate.

h3. Current notice:

(This is visible at the top of the work to the creator of the work while viewing/editing; for anyone else following a direct link to the work, this is all they see)

{{This work is part of an ongoing challenge and will be revealed soon! You can find details here: [COLLECTION LINK]}}

h3. Current description in blurbs:

{{This is part of an ongoing challenge and will be revealed soon!}}

h3. Proposed notice text (2 options):

h4. If a work is in a single, unrevealed collection *_AND_* that collection has a defined Reveal Date:

{{This work is part of an ongoing challenge and is scheduled to be revealed on [DATE]. Please visit [COLLECTION LINK] for details.}}

{{To learn more about unrevealed collections, check out <a href="/faq/collections#collectionoptions">What does it mean that a collection is Open or Closed, Moderated or Unmoderated, Unrevealed, or Anonymous?</a> in our <a href="/faq/collections">Collections FAQ</a>.}}

h4. All other options (no defined date, multiple collections, etc.):

{{This work is part of a collection that has not been revealed. Please visit [COLLECTION LINK] for details.}}

{{To learn more about unrevealed collections, check out <a href="/faq/collections#collectionoptions">What does it mean that a collection is Open or Closed, Moderated or Unmoderated, Unrevealed, or Anonymous?</a> in our <a href="/faq/collections">Collections FAQ</a>.}}

h3. Proposed blurb description:

{{This work is part of a collection that has not been revealed.}}

h3. Note:

We should start using {{to_sentence}} for the collection links (so it would be like "Title 1 and Title 2" when there are two and "Title 1, Title 2, and Title 3" when there are 3+), since right now we're using a simple join that's not good for i18n.
